  "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{4}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{2+1}}{2+1}{|}_{-5}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{-5}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(-5)^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{3}+\\frac{125}{3} \\\\  & =63.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
